   135	
   136	## Issuance lifecycle (2026-10-30)
   137	
   138	Implements `docs/decisions/2026-10-29-issuance-lifecycle.md` (revision 5.3.1) and its "Implementation boundary until
   139	the author decides"; the checked protocol is `formal/tla/issuer-lifecycle/IssuerLifecycleR53.tla`. Tests:
   140	`tests/test_lifecycle.py` (one group per brief item); deadline tests in `test_faults.py`, `test_review_fixes.py`,
   141	`test_confirm_fixes.py`, `test_states.py` and `test_infra.py` are rewritten and say so in their docstrings.
   142	
   143	- **Attempts** (`tessera_issue/lifecycle.py`): a request has attempts 1..3 (`attempts`, `cur`). Each has its own
   144	  declared issue time (its allocation time), frames, signing jobs (request ids scoped by attempt), A_sig, a fresh stamp,
   145	  evidence, latch and end; its objects live under `work/<rid>/a<n>/`. A signer response is routed by attempt; one for
   146	  an attempt that is not current is logged `other-attempt` and ignored.
   147	- **One writer.** Only the poller makes lifecycle transitions. `api.status` and `api.receipt` write nothing; `settle`
   148	  and `fail_after` are gone. Every poller write is guarded on (request state, current attempt id, current attempt
   149	  state) and the version (`stores.lifecycle_guard`; DynamoDB conditions on the item attributes `lstate`, `latt`,
   150	  `lastate` and `version`).
   151	- **Fence.** Before fetching evidence for an attempt (stages `evidence`, `finalize`, `snapshot`), the poller commits a
   152	  guarded version bump and proceeds only if it committed.
   153	- **Eligibility and latch.** The attempt's proof must stamp SHA-256 of its own A_sig; the verifier's `select` picks the
   154	  lowest qualifying height among attestations whose full pinned, linked h..h+5 segment was obtained; the three A2.2
   155	  conjuncts are evaluated on it. On eligibility, at any time while the attempt is open, the poller writes the
   156	  presentation (proof pruned to the selected height, with its six headers) as an immutable digest-named object, then
   157	  commits the latch with `observed_at` and its reference.
   158	- **Ending.** Only complete negative evidence (every stamped calendar attested, every attestation's segment obtained,
   159	  the selected presentation failing a conjunct) ends an open attempt: DISCARDED at or before B, EXPIRED after it.
   160	  The end and the next attempt's allocation are one guarded write; after attempt 3 the same write records REFUSED
   161	  `ATTEMPTS_EXHAUSTED`; if the next attempt would need signing after the stop, REFUSED `SIGNING_CLOSED`. A signer
   162	  refusal discards that (unsigned) attempt the same way.
   163	- **After the latch** (step 7; ILI-01, ILI-02). Transient failures are retried indefinitely. The pre-ship check returns
   164	  the verifier's per-row ledger, and `pipeline.classify_preship` classifies the first failing check by what it depends
   165	  on: an INVALID check on frozen material (the attempt's frames, frozen signatures, A_sig, manifest and keys; the
   166	  preserved receipt presentation, rows 11.x-12.x, including OTS_MERKLE_MISMATCH and the transaction-shape/txid check;
   167	  the window's frozen git material, rows 14.1-14.6 and 14.8; 16.1) discards the attempt with reason
   168	  `PRESHIP:INVALID/<code>@<row>`; a snapshot failure (13.x, 15.x) recaptures the snapshot; anything else (headers and
   169	  pins, container, catalog and trust configuration, every UNVERIFIABLE result) is retried. T > not-after discards
   170	  (`T_AFTER_NOT_AFTER`). A snapshot failure discards (`SNAPSHOT_IMPOSSIBLE`, with the evidence) only when no lawful
   171	  snapshot can be obtained any more, proven from evidence: the current snapshot's evidence is complete, and the median
   172	  time past of the eleven authenticated headers ending five below the tip is later than declared + delta, so every
   173	  future anchor fails row 13.7. Elapsed time never discards.
   174	- **Open termination concern (outside the step-5 gate).** Where impossibility cannot be proven, a latched attempt is
   175	  retried without end: for example a DNS record that stays wrong (15.x) while the chain's median time past has not
   176	  passed declared + delta, a trust-configuration or catalog failure the operator never repairs, or a preserved
   177	  presentation object lost from storage. These are not sampled evidence unavailability, so the pending step-5
   178	  decision does not cover them; they leave A2.3's termination obligation unmet in those cases, and an author or owner
   179	  rule is needed if they must end.
   180	- **Presentation** (ILI-01, ILI-06). The latched presentation keeps only branches at the selected height whose
   181	  attested message is that block's merkle root; contradicted branches there are dropped (counted in the latch as
   182	  `contradicted_pruned`) and the pruned presentation is re-checked contradiction-free. Complete evidence in which every
   183	  attestation is contradicted ends the attempt `EVIDENCE_CONTRADICTED` (discarded at or before B, expired after);
   184	  incomplete or non-qualifying evidence stays open (ILI-03).
   185	- **Signing closure** (ILI-04). Durable signatures (stored and logged "used") are reconciled before closure is
   186	  decided; a complete recovered set is sealed whatever the window.
   187	- **Content** (ILI-08). Content is checked before attempt 1 is allocated (`FAILED CONTENT_UNAVAILABLE`, no attempt).
   188	  After allocation, lost content is recovered from an earlier attempt's attestation frame (it carries the bytes);
   189	  if none decodes to the content digest, no attempt can ever be built, and the ending write discards the attempt and
   190	  refuses the request `REFUSED CONTENT_UNAVAILABLE` (end-and-refuse, like `SIGNING_CLOSED`).
   191	- **Invocation budget** (ILI-05). Each poll has a budget (240 s of the 300 s Lambda timeout, lowered to the time the
   192	  invocation has left). A unit of remote work (a tip, one header height, one calendar request, a pre-ship check) starts
   193	  only if its worst-case cost fits; headers are checkpointed per height under `work/<rid>/<attempt>/hdr/`, calendar
   194	  upgrades are stored as they arrive, and an invocation out of budget makes no lifecycle decision and resumes next
   195	  poll. Requests are served round-robin from a durable cursor (`POLLER#cursor`), moved before each request is worked
   196	  on. Load is never shed by ending attempts.
   197	- **Bounded external fields** (ILI-07). Signer request ids, statuses and reasons are validated; an unrecognised or
   198	  oversized reason becomes `UNRECOGNIZED_REASON` and the original is stored by reference (`diag-<sha256>`, with its
   199	  digest and length). The DynamoDB fake rejects items over 400 KiB.
   200	- **GATED.** `EVIDENCE_UNAVAILABLE` is not implemented in any form. An attempt whose evidence never completes stays
   201	  open. `unavailable_since` and `failed_intervals` (runs of `fetch_start // 600`) are written for diagnosis only.
   202	  Nothing here claims termination.
   203	- **Storage.** No age rule applies to live objects: the S3 lifecycle rule expires only objects tagged `cleanup-due`,
