OMMITTED_BYTES_REASONS as the post-latch incurable set (find it in the code) — complete and correct?; (d) a latched attempt whose DNS snapshot can never be anchored by declared + δ stays latched forever — is that failure in fact incurable (so step 7 should discard with a recorded reason), and does leaving it open violate A2.3 termination outside the author's gate?; (e) FAILED CONTENT_UNAVAILABLE before any attempt; (f) SIGNER_REFUSED discards the attempt and allocates the next; (g) failed_intervals stored as capped runs (diagnostic only). (4) Tests: do the new tests mirror the model's interleavings, and would they fail against plausible bugs (the implementer ran a mutation plugin at /tmp/claude-1000/-home-tony-projects-tessera/5337431d-45fd-4acb-b9ce-1c8b7e135d0f/scratchpad/mut.IX4v/mutplug.py; it reports presentation pruning removal stayed green)? (5) AWS: DynamoDB item size, transaction use, Lambda 300 s budget with a fence write per evidence poll per request, S3 tagging permissions. Number findings ILI-01... with severity, file:line, concrete failure scenario, fix. One-line verdict: ready for deployment work (with the gate closed) or not. Apply these owner prechecks to the change (DESIGN.md and code comments included), PASS/FAIL with file:line:
