docs/reviews/issuer-lifecycle-impl/codex.log:8866:| Eligibility | Own `A_sig` digest, k=6, full linked segments and all three inclusive conjuncts are checked. Invalid-proof classification has ILI-01/03 gaps. |
docs/reviews/issuer-lifecycle-impl/codex.log:8868:| Negative endings | Partial, stale, failed and pending fetches do not cause expiry. Complete-invalid evidence needs ILI-03’s distinction. |
docs/reviews/issuer-lifecycle-impl/codex.log:8873:**The sampled-unavailability gate is closed.** No lifecycle path produces `EVIDENCE_UNAVAILABLE`, reads diagnostic failure history to decide an ending, or turns an evidence-stage timeout/age/signing closure into an equivalent ending. Stamped and latched attempts survive signing closure. ILI-04 and ILI-08 are separate pre-stamp ending defects, not evidence that step 5 has secretly been enabled.
docs/reviews/issuer-lifecycle-impl/codex.log:8879:| **(a) Latch the passing presentation in hand; prune to its height** | **Sound for the shipped presentation**, subject to ILI-01/06. Profile §7.1 selects among qualifying branches in the presented proof; a missing lower segment supplies no time fact. Pruning prevents later assembly headers changing that presentation’s selection. This is not owner acceptance of the policy. |
docs/reviews/issuer-lifecycle-impl/codex.log:8880:| **(b) Complete evidence with no qualifying attestation remains open** | **Too broad.** Incomplete qualification remains open; complete authenticated contradiction is conclusive invalidity. ILI-03. |
docs/reviews/issuer-lifecycle-impl/codex.log:8881:| **(c) `COMMITTED_BYTES_REASONS`** | Listed members are defensible; **the set is incomplete**, and reason-only classification needs provenance. ILI-01. |
docs/reviews/issuer-lifecycle-impl/codex.log:8882:| **(d) Permanently impossible snapshot remains latched** | **Incorrect under the stated impossibility premise.** Step 7 should discard with evidence and reason. Elapsed wall time or one `SNAPSHOT_TIME` result does not establish that premise. ILI-02. |
docs/reviews/issuer-lifecycle-impl/codex.log:8883:| **(e) `FAILED/CONTENT_UNAVAILABLE` before any attempt** | Defensible for an abandoned upload. The implementation also applies it after allocation. ILI-08. |
docs/reviews/issuer-lifecycle-impl/codex.log:8889:For AWS, ordinary bounded attempt metadata and S3 presentation references avoid embedding large proofs in DynamoDB; ILI-07 remains the size hole. Request creation correctly uses a transaction for request plus tombstone. Cleanup’s obligation-before-terminal ordering is appropriate. `s3:PutObjectTagging` is granted to the poller at [main.tf:241](/home/tony/projects/tessera/service/issuer/infra/main.tf:241), matching the API’s required permission. [AWS tagging API](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/API/API_PutObjectTagging.html)
docs/reviews/issuer-lifecycle-impl/codex.log:8896:| **2. Trigger clause** | **FAIL** | [pipeline.py:412](/home/tony/projects/tessera/service/issuer/tessera_issue/pipeline.py:412) applies signing closure before establishing that signing is still required. Durable recovery can falsify that antecedent—ILI-04. |
